# §1. Optimized-μ algebra: VERIFIED

With \(A=(|z|+r|c_{13}|/2)F\), \(B=r|c_{04}|F^2/2\), \(F=|a|/8+r|c_{31}|/48\),

\[
C_\mu=\frac{|w|}2+\frac{r|c_{22}|}8+\mu+\frac A\mu+\frac B{\mu^2},
\qquad
\frac{dC_\mu}{d\mu}=1-\frac A{\mu^2}-\frac{2B}{\mu^3}.
\]

Setting the derivative to zero and multiplying by \(\mu^3\) gives
\(\mu^3-A\mu-2B=0\) — **GP-AUD-042's equation, confirmed.** Uniqueness of the
positive root: \(g(\mu)=\mu^3-A\mu-2B\) has \(g(0)=-2B\le0\) and is strictly
increasing past \(\sqrt{A/3}\), so exactly one sign change on \((0,\infty)\)
whenever \(A+B>0\). Degenerate edge: \(A=B=0\) (i.e. \(F=0\), no transverse
forcing) makes \(C_\mu\) minimized only in the \(\mu\downarrow0\) limit — but
then the axis is invariant and no strip is needed; the criterion should simply
bypass root-finding there.

# §2. The closed polynomial majorant (the requested deliverable)

**Choose \(\hat\mu=\sqrt A+(2B)^{1/3}\).** No root-finding; every quantity is an
explicit jet polynomial/radical. Since the strip lemma holds for *every*
\(\mu>0\), \(C_{\hat\mu}\) is a valid sufficient threshold, and:

\[
\frac A{\hat\mu}\le\frac A{\sqrt A}=\sqrt A,
\qquad
\frac B{\hat\mu^2}\le\frac B{(2B)^{2/3}}=2^{-2/3}B^{1/3},
\]

so

\[
\boxed{\;C_{\text{closed}}
=\frac{|w|}2+\frac{r|c_{22}|}8
+2\sqrt A+\tfrac32\,2^{1/3}B^{1/3}
\;\ge\;C_{\hat\mu}\;}
\]

with \(\tfrac32 2^{1/3}\approx1.8899\).

**Optimality guarantee.** \(C_{\min}\ge\text{base}+\max\{2\sqrt A,\;
\tfrac32 2^{1/3}B^{1/3}\}\) (each from minimizing the two-term subproblems), and
the max of two nonnegative numbers is at least half their sum, so

\[
C_{\text{closed}}-\text{base}\;\le\;2\,(C_{\min}-\text{base}).
\]

**Never worse than a factor 2 beyond the optimum, fully closed-form** — and in
the pure-cubic case \(B=0\), \(\hat\mu=\sqrt A\) is *exactly* the optimizer:

\[
C_{\text{closed}}^{\text{cubic}}
=\frac{|w|}2+2\sqrt{\frac{|a||z|}8}
=\frac{|w|}2+\sqrt{\frac{|a||z|}2}.
\]

Independent cross-check: I reached \(\sqrt{|a||z|/2}\) separately this round via
the Riccati real-equilibrium condition on \(sY+F+\tfrac z2Y^2\) (discriminant
\(s^2\ge2|z|F\), with a factor-\(\sqrt2\) transient margin) — two routes, same
threshold shape. Practical tightness: on GP-AUD-041's exact-law sample the
numerically optimized \(C_{\min}=2.1763\); the closed form lands within a
fraction of a percent whenever one of \(A,B\) dominates, which is the observed
regime.

**Evaluated on the three GP-AUD-032 escapes (pure cubic, so exact-optimal):**

| # | \(s\) | \(A=|a||z|/8\) | \(C_{\text{closed}}\) | \(s+C\) |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 1 | −1.42160 | 1.37725 | 2.37903 | **+0.95744** |
| 2 | −1.23510 | 1.92803 | 2.91327 | **+1.67817** |
| 3 | −1.31009 | 1.25457 | 2.27424 | **+0.96415** |

All three margins positive — consistent with GP-DER-037's μ=1 adjudication and
tighter on samples 1–3 than the μ=1 values (2.379 vs 2.409; 2.913 vs 3.064;
2.274 vs 2.288), as optimization should be. **The closed form can replace the
numerical μ-solve in GP-AUD-042's replay with zero loss of validity and a
bounded, usually negligible, loss of tightness.** One caution: 042's *joint*
criterion wants the largest feasible μ (narrow strip for transit), a different
optimization; \(\hat\mu\) targets the strip threshold only.

# §3. Theorem 4.1 (GP-DER-043) line-by-line: VERIFIED, one expositional gap

Checked and confirmed: the typed upper bound \(s<w/2-rc_{22}/8\) from
\(H_{M,22}<0\); the exact scaling \(W_r=r^4|D_MD_S|\mathbf1_{\text{type}}\); the
polynomial envelope on \(|D_MD_S|\); the polynomial-length s-integral; the GR
density factorization \(\phi_r\le K e^{-c\|U\|^2}\) via uniform marginal and
conditional-variance bounds; the +1+4−2 exponent ledger; Lemma 3.1's limit and
the closed form \(z_0=(b^2+2)\Phi(b/\sqrt2)+\sqrt2\,b\,\phi(b/\sqrt2)=
3.230979\) at \(b=6/5\) (re-verified, matches my DER-001-era check).

**The one gap, expositional not substantive:** Lemma 3.1 invokes dominated
convergence while both the integrand *and the measure* vary in r. The clean
one-line repair GR already licenses: write every expectation against fixed
Lebesgue measure using the density envelope
\(\phi_r(x)\le K_\ast e^{-c_\ast\|x-m_0\|^2}\) (uniform over \(r\le r_1\) from
the eigenvalue and mean bounds), and dominate
\(|W_r/r^2|\phi_r\) by a single integrable function. Nothing else in the proof
changes. Recommend adding that sentence before any promotion, so the theorem's
only named premise really is GR.

Also affirmed for the record: §8's point that the *maximum type mark* supplies
the upper interval endpoint is load-bearing — without it the s-integral is
half-infinite and the +1 power is lost. That observation should travel with the
theorem into any registry node.

